                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a835272-ca5b-303f-a745-74afbfa0f5fe",
                                        "entry_id": "eead9ca2-2b97-372b-bd1f-670fe3ca808c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (coffee) in a percolator or a drip coffeemaker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ed148ea-f6db-48f2-a91e-1a4e051359f5",
                                                "sense_id": "8a835272-ca5b-303f-a745-74afbfa0f5fe",
                                                "text": "I’ll perk some coffee."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd0c41fe-0278-341d-a181-5183b07a9e44",
                                        "entry_id": "eead9ca2-2b97-372b-bd1f-670fe3ca808c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of coffee: to be produced by heated water seeping (“percolating”) through coffee grounds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25fbce47-07f4-471a-89ae-67d59f43576c",
                                                "sense_id": "cd0c41fe-0278-341d-a181-5183b07a9e44",
                                                "text": "The coffee is perking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21b9eef2-67e6-4ec7-8897-f1ab17422a22",
                                                "sense_id": "cd0c41fe-0278-341d-a181-5183b07a9e44",
                                                "text": "While the coffee perked, she flipped idly through a gardening magazine and scanned an article on the war against aphids."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "perk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64e209e4-c725-37d1-a736-740ccca2baa0",
                                        "entry_id": "11fe075c-bb50-3c39-a3ce-5c3b15c17951",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A percolator, particularly of coffee."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "perk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcfd6508-f097-3f88-8179-2bdc1c0153ac",
                                        "entry_id": "e811b2e9-bfbf-3e85-8f3e-ee14217d4a0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make trim or smart; to straighten up; to erect; to make a jaunty or saucy display of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "953e24b2-92e8-4044-937b-84d407ba680e",
                                                "sense_id": "bcfd6508-f097-3f88-8179-2bdc1c0153ac",
                                                "text": "[the squirrel] whisks his brush\nAnd perks his ears, and stamps and scolds aloud"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66554c81-765d-4ac2-9fed-ab84e03380ec",
                                                "sense_id": "bcfd6508-f097-3f88-8179-2bdc1c0153ac",
                                                "text": "The blue jay was having a fit, and the sapsucker perked his bright-eyed little head at him not more than a dozen feet away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5686f2d1-7bd6-320a-b307-0dc21dd774cb",
                                        "entry_id": "e811b2e9-bfbf-3e85-8f3e-ee14217d4a0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To appear from below or behind something, emerge, pop up, poke out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb1287d0-adbf-4abd-8c30-8af4474b5976",
                                                "sense_id": "5686f2d1-7bd6-320a-b307-0dc21dd774cb",
                                                "text": "The heads of plants above the crack’d ground perk:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0befe6a-12f8-4060-aeaa-77cb648eb856",
                                                "sense_id": "5686f2d1-7bd6-320a-b307-0dc21dd774cb",
                                                "text": "A white Paris net sort of cap, glittering with spangles, and incircled by a chaplet of artificial flowers, with a little white feather perking from the left ear, is to be my head-dress."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a054d1f-b277-4672-bc4e-f7d0a64ca2cf",
                                                "sense_id": "5686f2d1-7bd6-320a-b307-0dc21dd774cb",
                                                "text": "1842, Robert Browning, “The Pied Piper of Hamelin” in Lyrics of Life, Boston: Ticknor & Fields, 1866, pp. 35-36, lines 152-153,\n[…] suddenly up the face\nOf the Piper perked in the market-place,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fdabe7d-5b3c-4b1a-952a-b5abde6e355b",
                                                "sense_id": "5686f2d1-7bd6-320a-b307-0dc21dd774cb",
                                                "text": "1937 Robert Byron, The Road to Oxiana, London: Macmillan, Part 4, “Kavar,” p. 159,\nA strong warm wind carried a sound of chopping with it and a rustle of dead plane-leaves; through those leaves perked the green crooks of young ferns."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1dd90a5d-6c86-3528-be9a-f904862a823c",
                                        "entry_id": "e811b2e9-bfbf-3e85-8f3e-ee14217d4a0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exalt oneself; to bear oneself loftily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2ba22c8-224f-4821-b82c-7e7d2a0b34a8",
                                                "sense_id": "1dd90a5d-6c86-3528-be9a-f904862a823c",
                                                "text": "1574, Arthur Golding (translator), Sermons of Master John Calvin, upon the Booke of Job, London: Lucas Harison and George Byshop, Sermon 38, The first upon the tenth Chapter,\nFor whereof commeth thys hypocrisie in the popedome, that men shall preache free will, merits, and satisfactions, and set vp their bristles in suche wise, and beare themselues in hande that they may come perking before God, yea and preace thither lyke shamelesse strumpets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91489161-1d61-4a6c-bd20-5dd4230a917b",
                                                "sense_id": "1dd90a5d-6c86-3528-be9a-f904862a823c",
                                                "text": "[…] our Lord had never any such design, to set up a sort of men in such distance above their brethren; to perk over them, and suck them of their goods by tricks […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "perk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83758068-5396-3252-a496-e7aee03c0655",
                                        "entry_id": "fb402dee-2025-37cd-b2fa-3337ccc1498d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Smart; trim; spruce; jaunty; vain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20cbb22e-7401-4d0f-93dd-b218e67a6145",
                                                "sense_id": "83758068-5396-3252-a496-e7aee03c0655",
                                                "text": "My ragged rontes all shiver and shake,\nAs doen high Towers in an earthquake:\nThey wont in the wind wagge their wrigle tailes,\nPerke as Peacock: but nowe it auales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63d3e614-df08-49be-b717-eb83c68a487c",
                                                "sense_id": "83758068-5396-3252-a496-e7aee03c0655",
                                                "text": "All, joy’d at th’ omen, their foundation laid:\nAnd in short time a perk new wall is made."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "perk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cab4eb5-5cd5-3265-b64d-ef915cc8f7fd",
                                        "entry_id": "3c392987-edf8-350f-89dd-a7b9baff319c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To peer; to look narrowly, sharply, or inquisitively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5fc6a19-2780-4d25-b0e3-ecaed4e74a5d",
                                                "sense_id": "9cab4eb5-5cd5-3265-b64d-ef915cc8f7fd",
                                                "text": "He is a tall, thin, bony man, with an interrogative nose, and little restless perking eyes, which appear to have been given him for the sole purpose of peeping into other people’s affairs with."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "649edd2e-00ce-3806-aaa4-7caaa7ad00f8",
                                        "entry_id": "3c392987-edf8-350f-89dd-a7b9baff319c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To examine thoroughly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "perk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "284f04b5-6b54-3865-97f4-d607ef1f8e15",
                                        "entry_id": "9f748774-2b31-3ae7-9579-375fcd96c1ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To perch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46face9a-03a8-42cc-b8a7-93b6b76da95d",
                                                "sense_id": "284f04b5-6b54-3865-97f4-d607ef1f8e15",
                                                "text": "His seconde hawke wexyd gery\nAnd was with flyenge wery.\nShe had flowyn so oft,\nThat on the rode loft\nShe perkyd her to rest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e348ce8-c25e-4028-be25-2a6d13c6de6e",
                                                "sense_id": "284f04b5-6b54-3865-97f4-d607ef1f8e15",
                                                "text": "Then sir, let me say, that Mineruas owle was proude, for perking vnder [h]ir golden target […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64cffd5b-94d7-4a05-95eb-625134f4c68c",
                                                "sense_id": "284f04b5-6b54-3865-97f4-d607ef1f8e15",
                                                "text": "O! what a ravishment ’thad beene, to see\nThy little Saviour perking on thy Knee!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1270ff26-dca9-4c58-888c-0ad6a32f159e",
                                                "sense_id": "284f04b5-6b54-3865-97f4-d607ef1f8e15",
                                                "text": "With respect to walking, it is the favourite exercise of my life; I sometimes divert myself with objects on the road, which, my being on a level with them, offers to observation; and yet, which, had I been perked up beyond my natural height on the back of a horse, would have been all overlooked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24cf6646-70a3-4aaa-ab41-6abd23a124d7",
                                                "sense_id": "284f04b5-6b54-3865-97f4-d607ef1f8e15",
                                                "text": "Laugh out in the loose green jerkin / That’s fit for a goddess to work in, / With shoulders brown, / And the wheaten crown / About thy temples perking."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4220b679-1e21-478c-a50c-b075cb4306d5",
